<title>FINLAND: ASKO SAYS TO DIVEST PART OF KARHU SPORT.</title>
<headline>ASKO SAYS TO DIVEST PART OF KARHU SPORT.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish plastic pipes, white goods and furniture maker Asko Oy said in a statement on Friday it would sell the cross-country skiing and footwear businesses of its Karhu Sport Oy unit to a group of investors.</p>
<p>The 1996 net sales of the operations to be divested are expected at 55 million markka, Asko said.</p>
<p>Neither the price nor other financial terms of the transaction were given in the statement.  </p>
<p>The operations to be sold employ about 30 people, it said.</p>
<p>The group of investors buying the business consists of Karinvest Oy -- owned by north Carelian cities, the state's Kera Oy and Sitra -- and part of Karhu Sport's management, Asko said.</p>
<p>&quot;Karhu Sport Oy will continue its Finnish baseball business in Askola,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-6805 0245</p>
